FlowLogsResponseSchema.description:
Response schema for GET /flows/{id}/logs - matches Rails flow_logs action.

Rails returns raw dataplane data with structure:
{
    "status": 200,
    "message": "Ok",
    "logs": {"data": [...], "meta": {...}}
}

Each log entry has: log, log_type, severity, resource_id, resource_type, timestamp

FlowMetricsResponseSchema.description:
Response schema for GET /flows/{id}/metrics - matches Rails flow_metrics action.

Rails returns raw dataplane data with structure:
{
    "status": 200,
    "message": "Ok",
    "metrics": {...}
}

PARITY: Rails renders `render status: result[:status], json: result` which
passes through whatever the MetricsService returns verbatim.  The status
field can be an int (200) or a string ("internal_server_error").

post.description:
Reset (replace all) accessors for a data schema.

Matches Rails POST /data_schemas/:id/accessors endpoint (AccessorsConcern, mode: :reset).
Expects: {"accessors": [{"type": "USER", "id": 123, "access_role": "collaborator"}]}

put.description:
Add accessor(s) to a data schema.

Matches Rails PUT /data_schemas/:id/accessors endpoint (AccessorsConcern, mode: :add).
Expects: {"accessors": [{"type": "USER", "id": 123, "access_role": "collaborator"}]}

get.description:
List linked flows for a flow.

Matches Rails flows#list_linked_flows.
Returns: {"linked_flows": [origin_node_id, ...]}

Rails ``active_config`` — GenAiConfigProvider walks four candidates.

A miss is **200** with ``{"message": "No active config found"}``, not a 404;
an invalid usage is a 400 raised by the provider's constructor.

